Please note that you need to have proper rights to create files and directories or it won't work.

Also, remember to handle potential errors. In this example, if there was an error while opening the file (for instance because of insufficient permissions), the `open` function returns -1 and sets `errno` accordingly. We check for that, print out the corresponding error message using `perror`, and return 1 from `main` to indicate an error occurred.
