        }
    }

    printf("Trimmed string: %s\n", str);
    return 0;
}
```
This code takes a single argument and trims any trailing whitespace or newline characters. It first checks that the program has been called with exactly one argument, then verifies that this argument is printable (i.e., consists entirely of visible characters), then trims trailing spaces, and finally converts newlines to spaces. If these checks fail, it prints an error message and exits.
